+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope; Narrowing the Directory Does Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for pets, visits, and veterinarians, leaving owners the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was ever decided stayed open.
+
+A request arrived on 2026-08-31 to narrow the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one specialty. It reads against the row two ways. As written, NG-9 covers it, because narrowing a list by a value is a kind of searching. Read against the row's rationale, it does not: the rationale declines repeating paged prefix search, and the directory already shows the specialty on every entry.
+
+The owner has now decided the row (2026-08-31).
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Read NG-9 as covering the request and decline it.** Rejected: the rationale that carries the row does not reach a filter over a value the page already prints. Declining on the row's letter would decline scope no one had decided to decline.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Rejected: free-text search over veterinarians, pets, or visits still repeats what owner search teaches, which is the reason the row exists.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by a specialty it already shows is not search under this row, and is in scope. Free-text search over veterinarians remains declined, as does search over pets and visits.
+
+The narrowing reaches the veterinarian directory alone. Narrowing another listing is its own decision, not one this row now permits by implication.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation in its narrowed form. Every other undecided row remains part of it.
+- REQ-VET-003 records the capability the narrowing admits, across both published forms of the directory.
+- A future request for free-text search over any entity proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake. The request itself never reopens the row.
+- The row is now two rules in one line: what is declined, and what was carved out. A later narrowing of another kind needs its own ADR rather than an edit to the rationale.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble naming it decided.
+- [REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
